      "output": "**Reading\u2011and\u2011Analysis Plan (12\u202fweeks)**  \n\n| Week | Core Goal | Primary Sources (type) | Output |\n|------|-----------|------------------------|--------|\n| 1 | Clarify research question & theoretical framing | \u2022 Recent review articles in *Journal of Urban Economics* (last 5\u202fy) <br>\u2022 Classic textbook chapters on agglomeration economies | One\u2011page problem statement with key hypotheses |\n| 2 | Map the empirical landscape | \u2022 Meta\u2011analyses of city\u2011level productivity studies <br>\u2022 Working papers from NBER/CEPR on spatial spillovers | Annotated bibliography (\u224815\u202fentries) highlighting data sets used |\n| 3 | Select data sources | \u2022 Government statistical portals (e.g., Census, Land Use) <br>\u2022 Commercial GIS datasets (e.g., OpenStreetMap) | Data inventory sheet with access notes and licensing constraints |\n| 4 | Review econometric methods for spatial panel data | \u2022 Methodology papers on SAR, SEM, and spatial\u2011Durbin models <br>\u2022 Software tutorials (R\u202fspdep, Stata\u202fspreg) | Code skeleton (data import\u202f+\u202fbasic descriptive stats) |\n| 5 | Pilot data cleaning & variable construction | \u2022 Raw data files identified in Week\u202f3 <br>\u2022 Documentation of variable definitions from literature | Cleaned dataset (subset of 10\u202fcities) and data\u2011dictionary |\n| 6 | Test baseline specifications | \u2022 Papers identified in Week\u202f2 that use OLS/IV <br>\u2022 Replication scripts (if available) | Replication notebook reproducing a key result (baseline model) |\n| 7 | Incorporate spatial dependence | \u2022 Spatial econometrics literature (Weeks\u202f4\u20115) <br>\u2022 Sensitivity\u2011analysis guidelines | Revised model with SAR/SDM, diagnostics table |\n| 8 | Robustness checks (alternative specifications, instruments) | \u2022 Studies employing different spatial weights, lag structures <br>\u2022 Instrumental\u2011variable applications in urban settings | Robustness report (3\u20134 alternative specs) |\n| 9 | Draft results section | \u2022 All model outputs from Weeks\u202f6\u20118 | Full results draft (tables\u202f+\u202finterpretive text) |\n|10 | Integrate theory & findings | \u2022 Theoretical papers from Week\u202f1 <br>\u2022 Discussion sections of top\u2011cited empirical works | Synthesis paragraph linking mechanisms to empirical evidence |\n|11 | Write introduction & conclusion | \u2022 Existing dissertations on related topics (university repositories) | Complete front\u2011matter (intro, lit\u2011review, conclusion) |\n|12 | Full revision & formatting | \u2022 Dissertation guidelines (your department) <br>\u2022 Reference manager export (e.g., Zotero) | Polished manuscript ready for submission |\n\n**Next actionable step (today):** Download the two most\u2011cited review articles from *Journal of Urban Economics* (last five years) and draft a one\u2011paragraph summary of how they frame agglomeration effects.  \n\n*Is there a particular data set you already have access to that should be prioritized in Week\u202f3?*",
