      },
      "output": "**Long\u2011weekend caf\u00e9\u2011focused break \u2013 Dublin, Ireland**  \nA short flight (\u22481\u202fh\u202f15\u202fmin) lets you avoid early departures, and the city\u2019s compact centre, vibrant coffee scene and walkable streets match your slow\u2011travel, one\u2011city style.\n\n**Day\u202f1 \u2013 Arrival & settle**  \nLate\u2011morning flight from Manchester to Dublin (choose a 10\u202fam\u2011ish departure). Check into a boutique hotel or well\u2011rated B&B in the Temple Bar/Smithfield area. Afternoon stroll to St\u202fStephen\u2019s Green, then unwind at **3FE Coffee** for specialty brews. Evening: casual dinner at **The Woollen Mills** with riverside views.\n\n**Day\u202f2 \u2013 Caf\u00e9 crawl & culture**  \nMorning (no early start) at **Brother Hubbard** on Capel Street. Mid\u2011day walk through the historic Trinity College Library (Book of Kells). Lunch at **The Fumbally** \u2013 relaxed, veggie\u2011friendly. Afternoon coffee at **Kaph** in the Creative Quarter, then explore the nearby Dublin Castle grounds. Evening: live music at **The Cobblestone** in Smithfield.\n\n**Day\u202f3 \u2013 Markets & parks**  \nLate\u2011morning brunch at **Two Pups Coffee** (South William Street). Browse the **George\u2019s Street Arcade** for local crafts. Lunch at **Balfes** for Irish comfort food. Afternoon tea\u2011style coffee at **Vice Coffee Inc.**, then a leisurely walk in Phoenix Park, maybe spotting the resident deer. Evening: dinner at **Delahunt** (modern Irish) and a nightcap at **The Vintage Cocktail Club**.\n\n**Day\u202f4 \u2013 Last sip & departure**  \nSleep\u2011in, then coffee at **Coffeeangel** near the river. Quick souvenir stop at **The Irish Design Shop**. Late\u2011morning flight back to Manchester (choose a 12\u2011pm\u2011ish departure to keep the day relaxed).\n\n**Cost drivers to verify**  \n- Flights: low\u2011cost carriers (Aer Lingus, Ryanair) \u2013 check prices 1\u20133\u202fmonths ahead.  \n- Accommodation: boutique hotels/B&Bs in central districts (\u00a3100\u2011\u00a3150 per night).  \n- Caf\u00e9 meals: \u00a35\u2011\u00a312 per coffee/ brunch; dinner \u00a315\u2011\u00a330 per person.  \n\n**Book now**  \n- Flight (to lock the late\u2011morning slot).  \n- Central accommodation (high demand for weekend stays).  \n\n**Decide later**  \n- Restaurant reservations (most are walk\u2011in friendly, but book The Woollen Mills if you prefer a guaranteed table).  \n- Any guided tours (e.g., literary walking tour) \u2013 optional.\n\n*Let me know if you\u2019d like alternatives (e.g., Edinburgh) or help with specific restaurant picks.*",
